# The key reference leaflet of Strata: landscape, three panels on each page.
# The panels follow what a user wants to do: moving, editing, copying and
# searching, then building a document, then the menus, files, printing and
# macros, then the keys of the markers, panels, lists and help, then the
# other programs.  Every key of the key list of the manual is on the
# leaflet, and every key on the leaflet is in that list.  A key is always a
# keycap.  The versions are marked with a word in italics, in parentheses,
# so that a mark cannot be taken for a key.
.doc Strata Key Reference
.landscape
.margins 0.2
.keyscale 0.9
.numbering off
.linespace 1.2
.h1 Strata key reference
.panels 33 35 33
= HOW TO READ THE KEYS
{k:Ctrl-A} | Hold Ctrl and press {k:A}.
{k:Alt-F2} | Hold Alt and press {k:F2}.
{k:Shift-Up} | Hold Shift and press {k:Up}.
{k:Keypad +} | The plus key of the numeric keypad.
{k:F12} {k:F} {k:S} | Press {k:F12}, then {k:F}, then {k:S}.
a letter | Press that letter.

= WORDS IN ITALICS
{i:(terminal)} | Only in the terminal version.
{i:(X11)} | Only in the X11 version.
{i:(Spell)} | Needs the spell check or the thesaurus.

= WHEN KEYS ARE HELD TOGETHER
{k:Shift-F1}..{k:Shift-F12} | Nothing.
{k:Ctrl-Alt-F2} {k:Shift-Alt-F2} | Same as {k:Alt-F2}.
{k:Ctrl-Up} {k:Alt-Left} {k:Alt-PgUp} | Same as the key without Ctrl or Alt.
{k:Ctrl-Shift-Left} | Holding Ctrl and Shift: Ctrl is used.
{k:Ctrl-Shift-Home} | Holding Ctrl and Shift: Shift is used.
{k:Shift-Del} {k:Ctrl-Del} {k:Alt-Del} | Same as Del.
{k:Ctrl-Ins} {k:Alt-Ins} | Same as Ins.
{k:Ctrl-Backspace} {k:Shift-Backspace} | Same as Backspace.
{k:Alt-A}..{k:Alt-Z} | Run the macro of that key.
.next
= MOVING THE CURSOR
{k:Left} {k:Right} | One character left, right.
{k:Up} {k:Down} | One line up, down.
{k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} {k:Ctrl-PgUp} {k:Ctrl-PgDn} | Half a screen up, down.
{k:Home} {k:End} | Start, end of the line.
{k:Ctrl-Left} {k:Ctrl-Right} | One word left, right.
{k:Ctrl-Home} {k:Ctrl-End} | Start, end of the block.
{k:Shift-Left} {k:Shift-Right} | One column left, right; at the edge, one
 level up, down.
{k:Shift-Up} | Headline of the section.
{k:Shift-Down} | Headline of the next section.
{k:Shift-PgUp} {k:Shift-PgDn} | Previous, next section of the same level.
{k:Shift-Home} {k:Shift-End} | Start, end of the document.
{k:Alt-F7} | Go To: start, end, a section number, next or previous section.

= DELETING AND BREAKING
{k:Del} | Delete the character under the cursor.
{k:Backspace} | Delete the character before.
{k:Ctrl-D} | Delete the next word.
{k:Alt-Backspace} | Delete the previous word.
{k:Enter} {k:Ctrl-M} {k:Ctrl-J} | Break the line.
{k:Tab} {k:Ctrl-I} | Insert a tab.
{k:Ctrl-Shift-Space} {k:Alt-_} | A space never broken at; a place to break a word.
{k:Ctrl-H} | Hanging indent.
{k:Alt-F5} {k:Alt-O} | Overtype on, off.
{k:Ctrl-/} {k:Ctrl-Z} {k:Ctrl-F10} | Undo.
{k:Alt-/} {k:Ctrl-F11} | Redo.

= LOOK OF THE TEXT
{k:Ctrl-B} | Bold on, off.
{k:Alt-I} | Italics on, off ({k:Ctrl-I} is Tab).
{k:Ctrl-U} | Underscore on, off.
{k:Ctrl-N} | Normal text.
{k:Alt-F6} | Attribute menu.
{k:Ctrl-F2} | Math: calculate numbers.
{k:Ctrl-F6} | Case: upper, lower or capitalize.
.next
= COPY, CUT, PASTE AND MOVE
{k:F3} | Copy: choose Text, Column, Block or Section, highlight it, press
 Enter.
{k:F4} | Cut: the same.
{k:F7} | Move: the same, put the cursor where it goes, press {k:F5}.
{k:F5} | Paste at the cursor.
{k:Ctrl-X} | Cut text: highlight it, press Enter.
{k:Alt-F4} | Delete: choose, highlight, press Enter.
{k:Ctrl-F3} | Copy to the library, under a name.
{k:Ctrl-F4} | Cut to the library, under a name.
{k:Ctrl-F5} | Paste from the library: choose from a list.

= WHILE TEXT IS HIGHLIGHTED
cursor keys | Stretch the highlight.
{k:Enter} | Accept it.
{k:Esc} | Cancel it.
{k:F1} | Help.
{k:Home} {k:End} | Sorting a table: start, end of the section.
{k:+} {k:-} | Sorting a table: change the direction.

= SEARCH AND REPLACE
{k:F9} | Search: type the text, press Enter.
{k:Alt-F9} | Replace: asks at each place;
 {k:A} changes all.
{k:Ctrl-F9} | Search again, the same way.
{k:Ctrl-F8} {k:Ctrl-F7} | Next, previous Print Error.
.end
.pagebreak
.panels 33 35 33
= BLOCKS AND COLUMNS
{k:Ctrl-A} | Append a block with the format of this one.
{k:Ctrl-O} | Append a block with the global format.
{k:Alt-F2} | Append menu: Column, Block, Global-block, Peer-section,
 Sub-section.
{k:F2} | Split menu: Column, Block, Section.
{k:Ctrl-V} | Split the block at the cursor.
{k:Alt-F3} | Join menu: Block, Section.
{k:Ctrl-K} | Cut the block; {k:F5} pastes it.
{k:F8} | Table menu: Add column, Split column here.
{k:F6} {k:Ctrl-E} | Block format: indent, justification, tabs, and more.

= SECTIONS
{k:Ins} {k:Ctrl-Ins} {k:Alt-Ins} | Append a section of the same level.
{k:Shift-Ins} | Append a subsection.  A terminal may keep this key: use
 {k:Alt-F2}, then Sub-section.
{k:Ctrl-Y} | Split the section at the cursor.
{k:Ctrl-L} | Cut the section.
{k:Ctrl-^} | Edit this section only; again: the whole document.

= OUTLINE AND LEVELS
{k:Alt-1}..{k:Alt-9} | Show headlines down to that level; again: back.
{k:Alt-0} | Outline the document; again: open all.
{k:Keypad +} {i:(X11)} | Expand the section; again: one level deeper.
{k:Alt-+} {k:Alt-=} {i:(terminal)} | The same.
{k:Keypad -} {i:(X11)} {k:Alt--} {i:(terminal)} | Collapse the section.
{k:Keypad *} {i:(X11)} {k:Alt-*} {i:(terminal)} | Show, hide its text.
{k:Alt-[} {k:Alt-<} {k:Alt-,} | Move the section left, up a level.
{k:Alt-]} {k:Alt->} {k:Alt-.} | Move the section right, down a level.
 ({k:Alt-[} does not work in a terminal.)
.next
= MENUS
{k:F12} | The menu bar; press again to leave it.
{k:Left} {k:Right} | Previous, next entry.
{k:Home} {k:End} | First, last entry.
{k:Enter} {k:Ins} {k:Down} | Open the entry.
{k:Esc} | Back one level; at the top, leave.
a letter | The entry that begins with it.
{k:Ctrl-F} {i:(terminal)} | A list of the Alt-F commands.

= WHERE THE COMMANDS ARE
File | Save, Retrieve, New, Delete, Import, Export
Global | Format, Page, Typeface, Marker, Options, Named (Edit, Delete)
Edit | Title, Structured or Unstructured, Section or Document, Window,
 Block, Parts, Layout, Insert
Print | Draft, Final, Preview (Document, Block, Section), Errors (Next,
 Previous, Remove, Remove All)
Tools | Macros (Edit, Delete, Learn, Save, Retrieve), Library (Edit, Delete,
 Save, Retrieve, Copy, Cut, Paste), Spell, Thesaurus, Autosort (Section,
 Table), Count, Undo, Redo, Find (Search, Replace, Again, Go To), Math
Help | The help of the edit screen
Quit | Leave the Editor

= FILES
{k:Ctrl-S} | Save ({k:F12} {k:F} {k:S}).
{k:Ctrl-R} | Retrieve a file ({k:F12} {k:F} {k:R}).
{k:Ctrl-Q} | Leave the Editor ({k:F12} {k:Q}).
New, Delete, Import, Export | {k:F12} {k:F}, then {k:N}, {k:D}, {k:I} or {k:E}.

= PRINTING AND PREVIEW
{k:Ctrl-P} | Print, final quality ({k:F12} {k:P} {k:F}).
Draft | {k:F12} {k:P} {k:D}.
Preview | {k:F12} {k:P} {k:P}, then {k:D} document, {k:B} block or {k:S}
 section.  In the X11 version the Viewer opens.
{k:Esc} | Stop while LaTeX works.
.next
= MACROS AND LIBRARY
{k:Alt-A}..{k:Alt-Z} {k:Alt-0}..{k:Alt-9} | Run the macro of that key.
{k:Ctrl-F1} | Learn: start or end a recording.
Learn | {k:F12} {k:T} {k:M} {k:L}: type the key, a note, then the text.
Macros | Edit {k:E}, Delete {k:D}, Save {k:S}, Retrieve {k:R}
 (after {k:F12} {k:T} {k:M}).
Library | The same, after {k:F12} {k:T} {k:L}.

= FORMATS AND FONTS
{k:F6} {k:Ctrl-E} | Block format: indent, justification, tabs, and more.
Typeface | {k:F12} {k:G} {k:T}.
Format | {k:F12} {k:G} {k:F}; {k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} turn the pages.
Page, Marker | {k:F12} {k:G} {k:P}, {k:F12} {k:G} {k:M}.
Options, Named | {k:F12} {k:G} {k:O}, {k:F12} {k:G} {k:N}.
Font marker | {k:Alt-F12}, then Font.

= MORE OF THE MENU
Title | {k:F12} {k:E} {k:T}.
Edit mode | {k:F12} {k:E} {k:S}: Structured, Unstructured, Section or Document.
Sort a section | {k:F12} {k:T} {k:A} {k:S}.
Sort a table | {k:F12} {k:T} {k:A} {k:T}.
Count words | {k:F12} {k:T} {k:C}.
Spell | {k:F12} {k:T} {k:S}, then {k:D} document, {k:B} block, {k:S}
 section or {k:W} word.

= SPELL AND THESAURUS {i:(Spell)}
{k:Ctrl-C} | Spell the word.
In the spell panel | Accept, Define, Ignore, Edit, Guess, Line, Quit: press
 the first letter.
{k:Ctrl-T} | Thesaurus.
{k:Left} {k:Right} {k:Up} {k:Down} {k:Home} {k:End} | Walk the words.
{k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} {k:Ctrl-Home} {k:Ctrl-End} | Scroll; first, last.
{k:Enter} | Replace the word.
{k:Ctrl-T} {k:Ctrl-PgUp} | Look up, go back.
{k:Esc} | Leave.
.end
.pagebreak
.panels 33 35 33
= MARKERS
{k:Alt-F12} | On a marker: its panel.  Elsewhere: the Marker Commands.
{k:Ctrl-F12} {i:(terminal)} | The same.

= MARKER COMMANDS
{k:Up} {k:Down} {k:Left} {k:Right} | Move in the grid.
{k:Home} {k:End} | First, last command.
a letter | The next command that begins with it.
{k:Ins} {k:Enter} | Choose it; its panel opens.
{k:Esc} | Close the grid.

= NOTES AND EQUATIONS
A note, a comment or an equation opens an editor.
{k:Ins} | Keep the changes.
{k:Esc} | Restore the old text.
{k:Ctrl-W} {i:(X11)} | Show the equation as a picture; any key closes it.

= THE VIEWER {i:(X11)}
{k:n} {k:N} {k:Space} {k:PgDn} | Next page.
{k:p} {k:P} {k:PgUp} | Previous page.
{k:Home} {k:End} | First, last page.
{k:g} {k:G} | Go to a page: type the number, press Enter.
{k:Up} {k:Down} {k:Left} {k:Right} | Pan.
{k:+} {k:=} {k:Keypad +} | Zoom in.
{k:-} {k:Keypad -} | Zoom out.
{k:0} {k:Keypad 0} {k:Keypad *} | 100 percent.
{k:F1} {k:?} | Show, hide the keys.
{k:q} {k:Q} {k:Esc} | Close.
.next
= IN A PANEL
{k:Ins} | Accept the panel.
{k:Esc} | Cancel it.
{k:Down} {k:Tab} {k:Enter} | Next field.
{k:Up} {k:Shift-Tab} | Previous field.
{k:Left} {k:Right} | One character; in a choice: previous, next.
{k:Home} {k:End} | Start, end of the text.
{k:Backspace} {k:Del} | Delete (a field just entered: clear it).
any character | Type (a field just entered: replace the text).
{k:Space} | Next choice.
{k:F2} {k:Alt-+} {i:(terminal)} | A list of files, directories or choices.
{k:Keypad +} {i:(X11)} | The same.
{k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} | Next, previous page of a panel.

= IN A LIST
{k:Up} {k:Down} | Move.
{k:Home} {k:End} {k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} | First, last, a page up, down.
{k:Enter} | Choose.
{k:Esc} | Leave.
a letter | The next entry; in a short list, choose it.

= ONE-LINE QUESTION
{k:Enter} {k:Esc} | Accept, cancel.
editing keys | The first key replaces the old text.
any key | Closes a message.

= KEYPAD AND TERMINAL
{k:Keypad Enter} | Same as Enter.
{k:Keypad Home} {k:Keypad Ins} | With NumLock off: the key of the same name.
{k:Keypad 5} {k:Keypad .} | With NumLock on: a digit, the point.
Alt with a key {i:(terminal)} | Press Esc, then the key.  To use Esc alone,
 press it twice.
{k:Ctrl-F} {i:(terminal)} | A list of the Alt-F commands, for the terminals
 that keep those keys.
.next
= HELP
{k:F1} | Help.
{k:Tab} {k:Right} | Next link.
{k:Shift-Tab} {k:Left} | Previous link.
{k:Enter} | Follow the link.
{k:Backspace} {k:Ctrl-H} | Back; at the first topic, close.
{k:i} | Index of topics.
{k:Up} {k:Down} | One line.
{k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} {k:Space} | One page.
{k:Esc} {k:F1} {k:q} | Close help.

= DOCUMENT MANAGER
{k:Up} {k:Down} {k:Home} {k:End} | Move in the menu.
a letter | Select that entry.
{k:Enter} {k:Ins} | Run the entry.
{k:F1} | Help.
{k:Esc} | Close a menu.
In a form: |
{k:Ins} | Accept.
{k:Enter} | Next field; at the last: accept.
{k:Down} {k:Tab} {k:Up} {k:Shift-Tab} | Next, previous field.
{k:Esc} | Cancel.
{k:F2} {k:Alt-+} {k:+} {k:Keypad +} | A list of files.
any key | Closes a notice.

= TEXT PAGES
{k:Up} {k:Down} {k:PgUp} {k:PgDn} | Scroll.
{k:Space} {k:Home} {k:End} | Next page, first, last.
{k:Enter} {k:Esc} {k:q} {k:Ctrl-Q} | Close.
.end
.pagebreak
.panels 33 35 33
= THE KEYS ON THE EDIT MENU
{k:F1} | Help: {k:F12}, Help.
{k:F3} {k:F4} {k:F5} {k:F7} {k:Alt-F4} | Copy, Cut, Paste, Move, Delete:
 {k:F12}, Edit, Block.
{k:F2} {k:Alt-F3} {k:Alt-F2} | Split, Join, Append: {k:F12}, Edit, Parts.
{k:F6} {k:F8} {k:Alt-F6} {k:Alt-F8} {k:Ctrl-F6} | Format, Table, Attribute,
 Border, Case: {k:F12}, Edit, Layout.
{k:Ctrl-F12} {k:Alt-F5} | Marker, Overtype: {k:F12}, Edit, Insert.
.next
= THE KEYS ON TOOLS AND PRINT
{k:F9} {k:Alt-F9} {k:Ctrl-F9} {k:Alt-F7} | Search, Replace, Again, Go To:
 {k:F12}, Tools, Find.
{k:Ctrl-F2} | Math: {k:F12}, Tools, Math.
{k:Ctrl-F3} {k:Ctrl-F4} {k:Ctrl-F5} | Copy, Cut, Paste to the library:
 {k:F12}, Tools, Library.
{k:Ctrl-F7} {k:Ctrl-F8} | Previous, Next Print Error:
 {k:F12}, Print, Errors.
.next
= THE LETTERS OF THE MENU
Edit | {k:T} Title, {k:S} Structured or Section, {k:U} Unstructured, {k:D}
 Document, {k:W} Window, {k:B} Block, {k:P} Parts, {k:L} Layout, {k:I} Insert.
Tools | {k:M} Macros, {k:L} Library, {k:S} Spell, {k:T} Thesaurus, {k:A}
 Autosort, {k:C} Count, {k:U} Undo, {k:R} Redo, {k:F} Find.
{k:M} | Macros; Math is after Count: use {k:Right}.
{k:C} | In Block and in Library: Copy; Cut is next: use {k:Right}.
.end
